{"type":"message","id":"f95d33e8","parentId":"54ca7d3a","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:05.670Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-04 11:01 GMT+8] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: ## 任务：修复像素编辑器的 Encoding Bug\n\n### 当前状态\n项目已完成大部分开发，但 encoding 模块有 3 个测试失败。\n\n**工作目录**: `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n### 测试失败原因分析\n\n**问题1: Palette 索引问题**\n- Encoder 跳过了 index 0（保留给已删除像素）\n- Decoder 把前3个字节当作颜色读进去了\n\n**问题2: DataView 使用问题**\n- `data.buffer` 指向整个 ArrayBuffer，而不是当前 chunk 的数据\n\n### 你的任务\n\n1. **修复 `src/encoding/Decoder.ts`**\n   - Palette 解析时跳过前3个字节（dummy index 0）\n   - 确保 DataView 使用正确的 offset\n\n2. **运行测试验证**\n   ```bash\n   cd /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor && npm test\n   ```\n\n3. **确保所有 42 个测试通过**\n\n4. **输出报告到 `$HOME/.openclaw-reports/leader-agent/`**\n\n### 参考\n- Encoder 代码: 已跳过 index 0 (paletteData 前加3个 dummy 字节)\n- Decoder 代码: 需要对应跳过前3个字节"}],"timestamp":1772593265667}}
{"type":"message","id":"3b00db78","parentId":"f95d33e8","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:18.311Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to fix encoding bugs in a Pixel Art Editor project\n2. The workspace is `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n3. There are 3 failing tests in the encoding module\n4. The issues are:\n   - Palette index problem: Encoder skips index 0, but Decoder reads the first 3 bytes as color\n   - DataView usage problem: `data.buffer` points to the entire ArrayBuffer, not the current chunk\n\nMy tasks:\n1. Fix `src/encoding/Decoder.ts` - skip first 3 bytes when parsing palette, ensure DataView uses correct offset\n2. Run tests to verify\n3. Ensure all 42 tests pass\n4. Output report to `$HOME/.openclaw-reports/leader-agent/`\n\nLet me start by reading the Decoder.ts file to understand the current implementation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"我理解了任务：修复 PixelArtEditor 项目的 encoding 模块 bug。让我先查看当前代码和测试情况。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-db0b58cf1c1a42f781c3c8b238da7770","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/encoding/Decoder.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-edf4ee0a87124f69ada54feb6ebccfd6","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/encoding/Encoder.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-c436fd7d64754c0d9daa6f250a5d8490","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor && npm test 2>&1 | head -100"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":6755,"output":459,"cacheRead":9590,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16804,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772593265669}}
{"type":"message","id":"fd688562","parentId":"3b00db78","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:18.317Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-db0b58cf1c1a42f781c3c8b238da7770","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { PixelDataState, RGB } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/**\n * Decoder - Converts binary format to PixelData state\n */\nexport class Decoder {\n  #width = 0;\n  #height = 0;\n  #uuidTable: string[] = [];\n  #paletteTable: RGB[] = [];\n\n  /**\n   * Decode binary data to state\n   */\n  decode(data: Uint8Array): { state: PixelDataState; width: number; height: number } {\n    let offset = 0;\n\n    // Read magic number\n    const magic = String.fromCharCode(\n      data[offset],\n      data[offset + 1],\n      data[offset + 2],\n      data[offset + 3]\n    );\n    if (magic !== \"CRDT\") {\n      throw new Error(\"Invalid magic number\");\n    }\n    offset += 4;\n\n    // Read width and height\n    const view = new DataView(data.buffer);\n    this.#width = view.getUint16(offset);\n    this.#height = view.getUint16(offset + 2);\n    offset += 4;\n\n    // Read chunks\n    while (offset < data.length) {\n      const chunkId = String.fromCharCode(\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n        data[offset + 3]\n      );\n      const chunkLength = view.getUint16(offset + 4);\n      offset += 6;\n\n      const chunkData = data.slice(offset, offset + chunkLength);\n      offset += chunkLength;\n\n      switch (chunkId) {\n        case \"UUID\":\n          this.#decodeUUIDChunk(chunkData);\n          break;\n        case \"PLTT\":\n          this.#decodePaletteChunk(chunkData);\n          break;\n        case \"DATA\":\n          return {\n            state: this.#decodeDataChunk(chunkData),\n            width: this.#width,\n            height: this.#height,\n          };\n        default:\n          throw new Error(`Unknown chunk: ${chunkId}`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    throw new Error(\"Missing DATA chunk\");\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode UUID chunk\n   */\n  #decodeUUIDChunk(data: Uint8Array): void {\n    const uuidCount = data.length / 16;\n    this.#uuidTable = [];\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < uuidCount; i++) {\n      const offset = i * 16;\n      let hex = \"\";\n      for (let j = 0; j < 16; j++) {\n        hex += data[offset + j].toString(16).padStart(2, \"0\");\n      }\n      // Add hyphens back\n      const uuid = [\n        hex.substring(0, 8),\n        hex.substring(8, 12),\n        hex.substring(12, 16),\n        hex.substring(16, 20),\n        hex.substring(20),\n      ].join(\"-\");\n      this.#uuidTable.push(uuid);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode palette chunk\n   * Note: First 3 bytes are dummy (index 0 reserved for erased pixels)\n   */\n  #decodePaletteChunk(data: Uint8Array): void {\n    // Skip first 3 bytes (dummy at index 0)\n    const colorCount = (data.length - 3) / 3;\n    this.#paletteTable = [null as unknown as RGB]; // index 0 = null/erased\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < colorCount; i++) {\n      const offset = 3 + i * 3; // Skip first 3 bytes\n      this.#paletteTable.push([\n        data[offset],\n        data[offset + 1],\n        data[offset + 2],\n      ]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Decode data chunk\n   */\n  #decodeDataChunk(data: Uint8Array): PixelDataState {\n    const state: PixelDataState = {};\n    let offset = 0;\n    let x = 0;\n    let y = 0;\n    const view = new DataView(data.buffer);\n\n    while (y < this.#height && offset < data.length) {\n      const tag = data[offset];\n\n      if (tag === TAG_BLANK) {\n        // Blank run\n        const count = view.getUint16(offset + 1);\n        offset += 3;\n\n        // Skip blank pixels\n        for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n          x++;\n          if (x >= this.#width) {\n            x = 0;\n            y++;\n          }\n        }\n      } else if (tag === TAG_PIXEL) {\n        // Pixel\n        const writerId = data[offset + 1];\n        const timestamp = data[offset + 2];\n        const colorId = data[offset + 3];\n        offset += 4;\n\n        const key = `${x},${y}`;\n        const peerId = this.#uuidTable[writerId];\n        const color = colorId === 0 ? null : this.#paletteTable[colorId];\n\n        state[key] = [peerId, timestamp, color];\n\n        x++;\n        if (x >= this.#width) {\n          x = 0;\n          y++;\n        }\n      } else {\n        throw new Error(`Invalid tag: ${tag}`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    return state;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set height (deprecated, now read from INFO chunk)\n   */\n  setHeight(height: number): void {\n    this.#height = height;\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Data item types in run-length encoding\n */\nconst TAG_BLANK = 0;\nconst TAG_PIXEL = 1;"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772593278315}}
{"type":"message","id":"bd0aaaf9","parentId":"fd688562","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:18.322Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-edf4ee0a87124f69ada54feb6ebccfd6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { PixelDataState, RGB } from \"../types.js\";\n\n/**\n * Binary format constants\n */\nconst MAGIC = \"CRDT\"; // Magic number (4 bytes)\nconst CHUNK_INFO = \"INFO\"; // Info chunk identifier\nconst CHUNK_UUID = \"UUID\"; // UUID chunk identifier\nconst CHUNK_PLTT = \"PLTT\"; // Palette chunk identifier\nconst CHUNK_DATA = \"DATA\"; // Data chunk identifier\n\n/**\n * Data item types in run-length encoding\n */\nconst TAG_BLANK = 0; // Blank pixel (followed by run length)\nconst TAG_PIXEL = 1; // Colored pixel\n\n/**\n * Encoder - Converts PixelData state to binary format\n * Implements the 98% compression pipeline:\n * 1. UUID table deduplication\n * 2. Palette table deduplication  \n * 3. Run-length encoding\n * 4. Binary encoding\n */\nexport class Encoder {\n  #width: number;\n  #height: number;\n  #uuidTable: Map<string, number> = new Map();\n  #paletteTable: Map<string, number> = new Map();\n\n  constructor(width: number, height: number) {\n    this.#width = width;\n    this.#height = height;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode state to binary Uint8Array\n   */\n  encode(state: PixelDataState): Uint8Array {\n    // Build lookup tables\n    this.#buildTables(state);\n\n    const chunks: Uint8Array[] = [];\n\n    // Info chunk\n    chunks.push(this.#encodeInfoChunk());\n\n    // UUID chunk\n    chunks.push(this.#encodeUUIDChunk());\n\n    // Palette chunk (skip index 0 for erased pixels)\n    chunks.push(this.#encodePaletteChunk());\n\n    // Data chunk (run-length encoded)\n    chunks.push(this.#encodeDataChunk(state));\n\n    // Concatenate all chunks\n    const totalSize = chunks.reduce((sum, chunk) => sum + chunk.length, 0);\n    const result = new Uint8Array(totalSize);\n    let offset = 0;\n    for (const chunk of chunks) {\n      result.set(chunk, offset);\n      offset += chunk.length;\n    }\n\n    return result;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Build UUID and palette lookup tables from state\n   */\n  #buildTables(state: PixelDataState): void {\n    let uuidIndex = 0;\n    let paletteIndex = 1; // Start from 1, keep 0 for erased pixels\n\n    for (const key in state) {\n      const [peerId, , value] = state[key];\n\n      // Add to UUID table\n      if (!this.#uuidTable.has(peerId)) {\n        this.#uuidTable.set(peerId, uuidIndex++);\n      }\n\n      // Add to palette table (skip null/erased)\n      if (value) {\n        const hex = this.#rgbToHex(value);\n        if (!this.#paletteTable.has(hex)) {\n          this.#paletteTable.set(hex, paletteIndex++);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode INFO chunk: magic + width + height\n   */\n  #encodeInfoChunk(): Uint8Array {\n    const data = new Uint8Array(4 + 2 + 2); // 4 bytes magic + 2 bytes width + 2 bytes height\n    const view = new DataView(data.buffer);\n\n    // Magic number\n    data[0] = MAGIC.charCodeAt(0);\n    data[1] = MAGIC.charCodeAt(1);\n    data[2] = MAGIC.charCodeAt(2);\n    data[3] = MAGIC.charCodeAt(3);\n\n    // Width and height (big-endian uint16)\n    view.setUint16(4, this.#width);\n    view.setUint16(6, this.#height);\n\n    return data;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode UUID chunk: header + UUIDs\n   */\n  #encodeUUIDChunk(): Uint8Array {\n    const uuids = Array.from(this.#uuidTable.entries())\n      .sort((a, b) => a[1] - b[1])\n      .map(([uuid]) => uuid);\n\n    // Remove hyphens from UUIDs (36 chars -> 32 chars)\n    const uuidData = new Uint8Array(uuids.length * 16);\n    for (let i = 0; i < uuids.length; i++) {\n      const clean = uuids[i].replace(/-/g, \"\");\n      for (let j = 0; j < 32; j += 2) {\n        const byte = parseInt(clean.substring(j, j + 2), 16);\n        uuidData[i * 16 + j / 2] = byte;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Chunk: header (4 + 2) + data\n    const header = this.#encodeChunkHeader(CHUNK_UUID, uuidData.length);\n    const chunk = new Uint8Array(header.length + uuidData.length);\n    chunk.set(header, 0);\n    chunk.set(uuidData, header.length);\n\n    return chunk;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode palette chunk: header + colors (skip index 0)\n   */\n  #encodePaletteChunk(): Uint8Array {\n    const colors = Array.from(this.#paletteTable.entries())\n      .sort((a, b) => a[1] - b[1])\n      .map(([hex]) => this.#hexToRgb(hex));\n\n    // Skip index 0 by adding dummy bytes\n    const paletteData = new Uint8Array(3 + colors.length * 3);\n    paletteData[0] = 0; // Dummy R\n    paletteData[1] = 0; // Dummy G\n    paletteData[2] = 0; // Dummy B\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < colors.length; i++) {\n      const offset = 3 + i * 3;\n      paletteData[offset] = colors[i][0];\n      paletteData[offset + 1] = colors[i][1];\n      paletteData[offset + 2] = colors[i][2];\n    }\n\n    const header = this.#encodeChunkHeader(CHUNK_PLTT, paletteData.length);\n    const chunk = new Uint8Array(header.length + paletteData.length);\n    chunk.set(header, 0);\n    chunk.set(paletteData, header.length);\n\n    return chunk;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode data chunk with run-length encoding\n   */\n  #encodeDataChunk(state: PixelDataState): Uint8Array {\n    const data: number[] = [];\n\n    let x = 0;\n    let y = 0;\n\n    // Iterate through all pixels in row-major order\n    while (y < this.#height) {\n      const key = `${x},${y}`;\n      const pixel = state[key];\n\n      if (!pixel) {\n        // Blank pixel - count consecutive blanks\n        let blankCount = 0;\n        while (y < this.#height && !state[`${x},${y}`]) {\n          blankCount++;\n          x++;\n          if (x >= this.#width) {\n            x = 0;\n            y++;\n          }\n        }\n\n        // Write blank run (max 65535 blanks per run)\n        while (blankCount > 0) {\n          const count = Math.min(blankCount, 65535);\n          data.push(TAG_BLANK);\n          data.push((count >> 8) & 0xff);\n          data.push(count & 0xff);\n          blankCount -= count;\n        }\n      } else {\n        // Non-blank pixel\n        const [peerId, timestamp, value] = pixel;\n        const writerId = this.#uuidTable.get(peerId)!;\n        const colorId = value\n          ? this.#paletteTable.get(this.#rgbToHex(value))!\n          : 0;\n\n        data.push(TAG_PIXEL);\n        data.push(writerId);\n        data.push(timestamp);\n        data.push(colorId);\n\n        x++;\n        if (x >= this.#width) {\n          x = 0;\n          y++;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    const dataArray = new Uint8Array(data);\n    const header = this.#encodeChunkHeader(CHUNK_DATA, dataArray.length);\n    const chunk = new Uint8Array(header.length + dataArray.length);\n    chunk.set(header, 0);\n    chunk.set(dataArray, header.length);\n\n    return chunk;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Encode chunk header: 4-byte identifier + 2-byte length\n   */\n  #encodeChunkHeader(id: string, length: number): Uint8Array {\n    const header = new Uint8Array(6);\n    const view = new DataView(header.buffer);\n\n    header[0] = id.charCodeAt(0);\n    header[1] = id.charCodeAt(1);\n    header[2] = id.charCodeAt(2);\n    header[3] = id.charCodeAt(3);\n    view.setUint16(4, length);\n\n    return header;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Convert RGB to hex string\n   */\n  #rgbToHex(rgb: RGB): string {\n    return (\n      ((rgb[0] << 16) | (rgb[1] << 8) | rgb[2])\n        .toString(16)\n        .padStart(6, \"0\")\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Convert hex string to RGB\n   */\n  #hexToRgb(hex: string): RGB {\n    const num = parseInt(hex, 16);\n    return [(num >> 16) & 0xff, (num >> 8) & 0xff, num & 0xff];\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772593278320}}
{"type":"message","id":"e0fda0ec","parentId":"bd0aaaf9","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:19.373Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-c436fd7d64754c0d9daa6f250a5d8490","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"> pixel-art-editor@1.0.0 test\n> node --experimental-vm-modules node_modules/.bin/jest\n\nPASS tests/encoding.test.ts\nPASS tests/LWWRegister.test.ts\nPASS tests/PixelData.test.ts\nPASS tests/LWWMap.test.ts\n\nTest Suites: 4 passed, 4 total\nTests:       42 passed, 42 total\nSnapshots:   0 total\nTime:        0.568 s, estimated 1 s\nRan all test suites."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1043,"aggregated":"> pixel-art-editor@1.0.0 test\n> node --experimental-vm-modules node_modules/.bin/jest\n\nPASS tests/encoding.test.ts\nPASS tests/LWWRegister.test.ts\nPASS tests/PixelData.test.ts\nPASS tests/LWWMap.test.ts\n\nTest Suites: 4 passed, 4 total\nTests:       42 passed, 42 total\nSnapshots:   0 total\nTime:        0.568 s, estimated 1 s\nRan all test suites.","cwd":"/home/one/.openclaw/agents/leader-agent/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1772593279370}}
{"type":"message","id":"30e79637","parentId":"e0fda0ec","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:37.486Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"有趣！测试已经全部通过了（42 passed, 42 total）。这说明问题可能已经被修复了，或者我需要验证一下。\n\n让我检查一下 Decoder.ts 的代码是否已经正确修复了：\n\n1. **Palette 索引问题** - 查看 `#decodePaletteChunk` 方法：\n   - 代码显示 `// Skip first 3 bytes (dummy at index 0)`\n   - `const colorCount = (data.length - 3) / 3;`\n   - `const offset = 3 + i * 3; // Skip first 3 bytes`\n   - 这看起来已经正确跳过了前3个字节\n\n2. **DataView 使用问题** - 需要检查 `#decodeDataChunk` 和其他方法中的 DataView 使用：\n   - 在 `#decodeDataChunk` 中：`const view = new DataView(data.buffer);`\n   - 这确实是个问题！`data.buffer` 指向整个 ArrayBuffer，而不是当前 chunk 的数据\n   - 应该使用 `new DataView(data.buffer, data.byteOffset, data.byteLength)`\n\n但是等等，测试已经全部通过了。让我再仔细看看测试用例，看看是否真的覆盖了所有情况。\n\n不过按照任务说明，问题已经指出了 DataView 的问题。让我检查一下测试是否真的能捕捉到这个问题。\n\n实际上，如果 `data` 是通过 `data.slice()` 创建的，那么它可能会有自己的 buffer，此时 `data.buffer` 可能指向整个原始 buffer，而不是切片后的数据。\n\n这就是问题所在。虽然测试通过了，但我应该按照任务要求修复 DataView 的 offset 问题，确保代码的健壮性。我需要检查 `decode` 方法中 DataView 的使用情况，特别是在 `#decodeDataChunk` 和 `#decodeUUIDChunk` 方法中。\n\n在第15行左右创建的 DataView 可能存在同样的问题。我现在需要编写一个更全面的测试来验证当前的修复是否正确。既然所有测试都已通过，我应该检查测试文件来确认修复的范围和完整性。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"测试已经全部通过（42/42）。让我检查一下 Decoder 中 DataView 的使用是否已经正确修复："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-c0814820515a4c17afd15a229534b449","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/tests/encoding.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":3340,"output":862,"cacheRead":16343,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20545,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772593279373}}
{"type":"message","id":"359c1f39","parentId":"30e79637","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:37.495Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-c0814820515a4c17afd15a229534b449","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { Encoder, Decoder } from \"../src/encoding/index.js\";\nimport type { PixelDataState, RGB } from \"../src/types.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Encoder/Decoder\", () => {\n  describe(\"roundtrip encoding\", () => {\n    test(\"simple state encodes and decodes correctly\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {\n        \"0,0\": [\"alice-peer-id\", 1, [255, 0, 0]],\n        \"1,0\": [\"alice-peer-id\", 2, [0, 255, 0]],\n        \"0,1\": [\"bob-peer-id\", 1, [0, 0, 255]],\n      };\n\n      const encoder = new Encoder(2, 2);\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      decoder.setHeight(2);\n\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n      const { state: decoded } = decoder.decode(encoded);\n\n      // Check that all keys are present\n      expect(Object.keys(decoded)).toEqual([\"0,0\", \"1,0\", \"0,1\"]);\n\n      // Check values (peer IDs may differ, but values should be the same)\n      expect(decoded[\"0,0\"][2]).toEqual([255, 0, 0]);\n      expect(decoded[\"1,0\"][2]).toEqual([0, 255, 0]);\n      expect(decoded[\"0,1\"][2]).toEqual([0, 0, 255]);\n    });\n\n    test(\"handles null (erased) pixels\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {\n        \"0,0\": [\"alice\", 1, [255, 0, 0]],\n        \"1,0\": [\"alice\", 2, null], // Erased\n        \"0,1\": [\"bob\", 1, [0, 0, 255]],\n      };\n\n      const encoder = new Encoder(2, 2);\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      decoder.setHeight(2);\n\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n      const { state: decoded } = decoder.decode(encoded);\n\n      expect(decoded[\"1,0\"][2]).toBeNull();\n    });\n\n    test(\"handles blank pixels (missing keys)\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {\n        \"5,5\": [\"alice\", 1, [255, 0, 0]],\n      };\n\n      const encoder = new Encoder(10, 10);\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      decoder.setHeight(10);\n\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n      const { state: decoded } = decoder.decode(encoded);\n\n      expect(decoded[\"5,5\"][2]).toEqual([255, 0, 0]);\n    });\n\n    test(\"large state with many pixels\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {};\n      for (let y = 0; y < 10; y++) {\n        for (let x = 0; x < 10; x++) {\n          state[`${x},${y}`] = [\"alice\", 1, [x * 25, y * 25, 255]];\n        }\n      }\n\n      const encoder = new Encoder(10, 10);\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      decoder.setHeight(10);\n\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n      const { state: decoded } = decoder.decode(encoded);\n\n      expect(Object.keys(decoded).length).toBe(100);\n      expect(decoded[\"5,5\"][2]).toEqual([125, 125, 255]);\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe(\"compression ratio\", () => {\n    test(\"binary encoding is smaller than JSON\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {};\n      for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {\n        const x = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10);\n        const y = Math.floor(Math.random() * 10);\n        state[`${x},${y}`] = [\"alice\", i + 1, [Math.random() * 255, Math.random() * 255, Math.random() * 255]];\n      }\n\n      const jsonSize = JSON.stringify(state).length;\n      const encoder = new Encoder(10, 10);\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n\n      expect(encoded.length).toBeLessThan(jsonSize);\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe(\"run-length encoding\", () => {\n    test(\"encodes consecutive identical timestamps efficiently\", () => {\n      const state: PixelDataState = {};\n      for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n        state[`${i},0`] = [\"alice\", 1, [255, 0, 0]];\n      }\n\n      const encoder = new Encoder(20, 1);\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      decoder.setHeight(1);\n\n      const encoded = encoder.encode(state);\n      const { state: decoded } = decoder.decode(encoded);\n\n      // Should successfully decode all 20 pixels\n      expect(Object.keys(decoded).length).toBe(20);\n      for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n        expect(decoded[`${i},0`]).toBeDefined();\n      }\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe(\"error handling\", () => {\n    test(\"throws on invalid magic number\", () => {\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      const invalidData = new Uint8Array([0, 0, 0, 0, 10, 0]);\n\n      expect(() => decoder.decode(invalidData)).toThrow(\"Invalid magic number\");\n    });\n\n    test(\"throws on unknown chunk\", () => {\n      const decoder = new Decoder();\n      const data = new Uint8Array(16);\n\n      // Set magic number\n      data[0] = 67; // C\n      data[1] = 82; // R\n      data[2] = 68; // D\n      data[3] = 84; // T\n\n      // Set width\n      data[4] = 0;\n      data[5] = 10;\n\n      // Invalid chunk header\n      data[6] = 88; // X\n      data[7] = 88; // X\n      data[8] = 88; // X\n      data[9] = 88; // X\n      data[10] = 0;\n      data[11] = 0;\n\n      expect(() => decoder.decode(data)).toThrow(\"Unknown chunk\");\n    });\n  });\n});"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772593297493}}
{"type":"message","id":"722e9dd2","parentId":"359c1f39","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:01:52.867Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"测试已经全部通过，所有 42 个测试都通过了。让我检查一下 Decoder 中 DataView 的使用问题是否已经修复。从代码来看：\n\n1. 在 `decode` 方法中，有一行代码：\n```javascript\nconst view = new DataView(data.buffer);\n```\n\n这确实是一个问题，因为 `data.buffer` 指向的是整个 ArrayBuffer，而不是当前 chunk 的数据。但实际上让我再仔细看看：\n\n- `decode` 方法接收的 `data` 是 `Uint8Array`\n- `data.buffer` 是整个 ArrayBuffer\n- 当使用 `view.getUint16(offset)` 时，offset 是相对于整个 buffer 的\n\n但是，在实际使用中，这个 Decoder 似乎工作正常。让我看看是否有其他问题...\n\n实际上，我在看 Decoder 的 `#decodeDataChunk` 方法时发现问题：\n\n```javascript\n#decodeDataChunk(data: Uint8Array): PixelDataState {\n  // ...\n  const view = new DataView(data.buffer);\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n这里 `data` 是 chunkData（通过 `data.slice(offset, offset + chunkLength)` 得到的），所以 `data.buffer` 指向的是整个原始 buffer，而不是切片后的数据。\n\n但是等等，测试已经通过了，说明代码工作正常？让我再仔细分析一下...\n\n实际上 `Uint8Array.slice()` 返回一个新的 `Uint8Array`，它的 buffer 是原始 buffer 的一个视图，但是 offset 是相对于原始 buffer 的。\n\n\n这就导致了 `DataView.getUint16(offset + 1)` 读取的是原始 buffer 中的数据，而不是 chunk 的数据。不过测试全部通过，可能是因为在某些情况下代码仍然能够正常工作。需要确认一下代码是否已经被修复，或者 bug 是否仍然存在。让我检查 git 历史。\n\n现在所有测试都已通过，可以生成报告了。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"测试已全部通过！让我再验证一下 DataView 的使用问题是否已修复，并查看相关代码："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-d5ae703fdaad42f494a80f540eb50d9c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor && git log --oneline -5"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-14743759b2ae4c2ea656b5c3b33e32fb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor && git diff HEAD~1 -- src/encoding/Decoder.ts 2>/dev/null | head -50"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":1383,"output":820,"cacheRead":19681,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21884,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772593297495}}
