{"type":"message","id":"dbb9691b","parentId":"9e4b7e66","timestamp":"2026-03-04T03:03:36.605Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"现在让我创建报告文件。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-342e7dbfe1d14a2da419488ccb6b39ba","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw-reports/leader-agent/2026-03-04-encoding-bug-fix.md","content":"# Encoding Bug Fix Report\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-04\n**Task:** Fix PixelArtEditor encoding module test failures\n**Status:** ✅ Complete\n\n## Summary\n\nAll 42 tests are now passing. The encoding module bugs have been resolved.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nTest Suites: 4 passed, 4 total\nTests:       42 passed, 42 total\n```\n\n## Bug Analysis & Fixes Applied\n\n### Bug 1: Palette Index 0 Reserved for Erased Pixels\n**Issue:** Encoder skips index 0 (reserves it for erased/null pixels), but Decoder was not skipping the dummy bytes.\n\n**Fix in Decoder.ts (`#decodePaletteChunk`):**\n```typescript\n#decodePaletteChunk(data: Uint8Array): void {\n  // Skip first 3 bytes (dummy at index 0)\n  const colorCount = (data.length - 3) / 3;\n  this.#paletteTable = [null as unknown as RGB]; // index 0 = null/erased\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < colorCount; i++) {\n    const offset = 3 + i * 3; // Skip first 3 bytes\n    this.#paletteTable.push([\n      data[offset],\n      data[offset + 1],\n      data[offset + 2],\n    ]);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Corresponding Encoder behavior (`#encodePaletteChunk`):**\n- Adds 3 dummy bytes at the start of paletteData\n- Colors start at index 1\n\n### Bug 2: DataView Buffer Reference Issue\n**Potential Issue:** `data.buffer` could reference the entire ArrayBuffer when `data` is a slice.\n\n**Status:** After investigation, `Uint8Array.slice()` returns a new Uint8Array with its own buffer starting at byteOffset 0. The current implementation is correct.\n\n## Files Modified\n\n- `src/encoding/Decoder.ts` - Fixed palette decoding to skip index 0 dummy bytes\n\n## Test Coverage\n\nAll encoding tests pass:\n- Roundtrip encoding (simple state, null pixels, blank pixels, large state)\n- Compression ratio verification\n- Run-length encoding efficiency\n- Error handling (invalid magic, unknown chunks)"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":45,"output":507,"cacheRead":21341,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21893,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772593399484}}
